1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,256
1. Police officer signs in with password + one-time code

2
00:00:08,406 --> 00:00:10,069
The officer sees only the cases assigned to him

3
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:28,444
He registers a new case: Chain snatching, Kovai Road, Karur

4
00:00:28,594 --> 00:00:36,694
He files the FIR: it is hashed, encrypted and read by the local AI

5
00:00:36,844 --> 00:00:39,210
The AI recognises a FIR (100%) and extracts people, sections and amount

6
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:44,272
Verify integrity: the file matches the hash anchored on Hyperledger Fabric

7
00:00:44,422 --> 00:00:53,866
He also files the witness statement

8
00:00:54,016 --> 00:00:58,069
The case is shared with the district forensic lab (this case only)

9
00:00:58,219 --> 00:01:06,225
2. Forensic lab signs in

10
00:01:06,375 --> 00:01:12,225
It opens the shared case: the FIR and statement are NOT listed

11
00:01:12,375 --> 00:01:20,303
It can still file its own evidence: the forensic report

12
00:01:20,453 --> 00:01:23,850
Opening the officer's FIR directly returns Not found (access control)

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,850
Forensic sees only what it uploaded itself

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:39,491
3. Officer signs in again

15
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:46,975
Police now see the FIR, the statement and the forensic upload

16
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:54,928
4. District court judge signs in

17
00:01:55,078 --> 00:02:01,897
The case is already visible: judges of a district see all its cases

18
00:02:02,047 --> 00:02:06,475
The judge reviews all documents and details

19
00:02:06,625 --> 00:02:27,335
The judge records the verdict: Convicted, with sentence and reasons

20
00:02:27,485 --> 00:02:32,881
The judgment is filed like any evidence: hashed, encrypted, anchored on the ledger

21
00:02:33,031 --> 00:02:37,350
The case is now closed; the verdict cannot be edited

22
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:56,585
5. Now an attacker with database access alters the stored FIR

23
00:02:56,735 --> 00:03:02,146
Verify integrity now FAILS: the hash no longer matches the ledger

24
00:03:02,296 --> 00:03:12,350
6. The auditor (supervisor) reviews the audit trail

25
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:17,350
Every action on this case is logged: uploads, verdict, and TAMPER_DETECTED with who and when

26
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,881
The audit log itself is hash-chained: it verifies as intact

27
00:03:21,031 --> 00:03:27,584
The auditor independently re-checks the FIR: tampering detected, no content shown
